Independent review and qualification boundaries, 2026-10-01

The final production freeze is the five-file identity set in
metadata-batch-final-source-identities.log. Independent production review found
no remaining blocker in owner binding, accounting, fallback or sealed commit.
Two review findings were fixed before the final gates: reject a CRC-valid
equal-live tag on a committed root before optional refill, and require the
shared delete pending-free budget plus an initial older-root retirement slot.
The shared owner gate preserves sealing's original wrapper exclusions and
the qualified full-width stock versus narrowed old-leaf backup comparisons.

Independent test review verified the frozen functional, fault and sealed
fixture hashes and found no blocker. The two isolated guard-removal variants
each fail exactly their corresponding functional probe (15 passed, 1 failed),
while the frozen production passes all 16. The one-slot probe distinguishes
optional batch decline from successful ordinary allocation. The full-pending
fault test alone is only behavior-level fallback coverage: its zero writes and
AGAIN can also result from the ordinary B-tree headroom preflight.

Full/prefix first-write failures and full/prefix second-write failures are
tested with matching successful controls. The fragmented latter faults occur
after one successful actual Free-Tree COW/root swap. Published-root bytes,
volatile pool inventory, sticky recovery, no physical retry, and committed
checker/remount graph/data oracles are asserted. A later physical COW-write
failure is NOT a post-swap retirement-callback failure. No safe failure hook
was introduced for the real mounted callback. Source review establishes the
conditional valid-context argument: exclusive operation, exact owner-bound
sink tuple and successful headroom preflight leave no expected callback error
without owner-state corruption or forbidden reentry. Existing lower-level
atomic-root-shift retirement-failure tests also pass, but their substituted
sink is deliberately not eligible for the new batch. These facts do not prove
a batch-specific injected retirement failure or hardware flush honesty.

The sealed fixture repair uses an actual different-block leaf COW through an
active emergency scratch block, preserves all logical keys/values/free totals,
merges the returned old root into the saved reserve once, and retains the old
inactive historical-pool provenance assertions. It does not assert whole-node
byte identity, since transaction/checksum fields legitimately change. Some
test assertion-failure paths can bypass cleanup or unlock; successful paths
clean up and the full ASan/UBSan run passes (leak detection disabled as recorded).

Read-only Luna CRC audit found that the Amiga main loop already slices by four;
proposing slicing-by-four is not a new Amiga optimization. The ABI preserves
D2-D4/A2-A4, uses stack seed/data/length and D0 return, complements the initial
state and result, and handles zero length, arbitrary seeds and 0-3 byte tails.
CRC probe timing samples every 64th node call, not every buffer CRC invocation;
write timing includes the node checksum helper and zero-byte advancement.
A future assembly change needs actual 68k vector and callee-saved/stack ABI
runtime checks, not merely the portable host oracle. No CRC change was made.

All sixteen normal TSVs and both detailed probe orders were independently
extracted by Luna. Means, matched deltas, eighteen adverse observations,
twelve same-run threshold failures and the reported operation counts agree.
This is diagnostic/normal evidence agreement, not statistical precision.

Production and fixture changes were withdrawn with apply_patch from the exact
validated reverse diff; the new test files were compared with the saved evidence
then moved recoverably to build/metadata-batch-rejected-source. An initial
reverse-diff conversion rejected Git's reversed a/b header spelling before any
edit. The corrected conversion verified the exact six targets and completed.
The active production/fixture files match cb925e4; both retained patches pass
git apply --check there. The rejected implementation is not a retained speedup.
Raw unified patches preserve their required single-space blank context lines.
An evidence-local .gitattributes exempts only patch context-line end whitespace;
it does not alter source checks. Copied log final blank lines are normalized.
